# PM OS: Routing Rule (Hard Constraint)

<!-- CRITICAL_ROUTING_CONSTRAINT -->

For **any message** about strategy, decisions, opportunities, research, stakeholders, or meetings:

**Your first line of substantive output MUST be the routing declaration:**

```
ROUTING → [workflow name] | Reading: plugins/pm-workflows/agents/pm-workflows.md | Executing: plugins/pm-workflows/commands/workflows/[file].md
```

This declaration appears **after** the pre-flight block and **before** any advice, framework, or question.

After the declaration: ask **exactly one clarifying question**. No framework analysis. No strategic observations. Wait for the user to answer before proceeding.

## FAIL
```
[pre-flight block]
This is a classic prioritisation problem. The reversibility framework suggests...
ROUTING → Make Great Decisions | ...
What's your timeline?
```

## PASS
```
[pre-flight block]
ROUTING → Make Great Decisions | Reading: plugins/pm-workflows/agents/pm-workflows.md | Executing: plugins/pm-workflows/commands/workflows/make-great-decisions.md

Before I pull the right framework — which of these options, if you got it wrong, would be the hardest to reverse in six months?
```

**`/dev` mode does not exempt PM requests from routing.** No mode switch does.
